  "t1_semantics_note_A6": "merge-t1 is `rustkmer merge --num-threads 1` (CLI default is 0 = all cores). Per the PAR-01 pool contract (tests/thread_pool_size_tests.rs), a fresh CLI child at N=1 observes exactly 2 OS threads (N rayon workers + N engine workers + main at N=1) \u2014 the t1 row is a like-for-like single-worker scheduling point, NOT a one-OS-thread measurement. Observed here: merge-t1 medians run ~15-25% above the default merge arm at both k (e.g. B-k21 3.320s vs 2.890s; B-k31 3.560s vs 2.930s).",
  "roadmap_guardrail": "RSS is recorded as context only \u2014 no memory-win claim over the streaming jellyfish merge comparator is made from rehearsal evidence or summaries (jellyfish merge runs at ~6.8 MB RSS; the merge memory bar is 'below jellyfish' and already met). The rehearsal proves the harness pipeline, not a performance verdict; slice-scale walls and CVs are context for Phase-12 scheduling, with MBENCH-04's full-scale predicted-vs-measured check as the backstop.",
  "cv_warning_note": "cv_warning=True on some slice-scale arms (timer quantization on sub-second walls; jellyfish count arms show the widest spread). Warnings never fail a run by design; at slice scale they are expected and are part of the honest record.",
